Subject: [PATCH] avb: compare loaded partition result with its own enum

AvbPartitionData.verify_result has type AvbSlotVerifyResult. Both old and
new OK constants are zero; this is a type correction with no policy or
numeric change. It avoids Clang 21's -Wenum-compare error with PVMFW.
Applies to EDK2 aef4e86045bd151a54d33bab8ae5e8e62462a8f4.

diff --git a/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/AvbPopulateBccParams.c b/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/AvbPopulateBccParams.c
index 6bcbbaf..929f5f8 100644
--- a/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/AvbPopulateBccParams.c
+++ b/QcomModulePkg/Library/avb/AvbPopulateBccParams.c
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ PopulateBccParams (AvbSlotVerifyData *SlotData, BOOLEAN BootIntoRecovery,
         if (avb_strcmp (SlotData->loaded_partitions[LoadedIndex].partition_name,
                         "pvmfw") == 0 ) {
             if (SlotData->loaded_partitions[LoadedIndex].verify_result ==
-                AVB_VBMETA_VERIFY_RESULT_OK) {
+                AVB_SLOT_VERIFY_RESULT_OK) {
                 Status = PopulateBccImgParams (SlotData, bcc_params,
                                                LoadedIndex);
                 if (Status != EFI_SUCCESS) {
